WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:08.960
Even if producers at the History Channel knew
they'd struck gold when they cast the stars

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:14.639
of Mountain Men, they couldn't have predicted
just how rich the vein they'd hit.

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:20.011
Here are just a few tidbits of trivia that
never made it to television screens, all about

00:00:20.011 --> 00:00:22.640
the toughest guys in the world.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.480
Eustace Conway's School Beef

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:31.210
Inspired by Henry David Thoreau, Eustace Conway
ran his North Carolina-based nature school

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.609
on his own property for over two decades without
incident.

00:00:35.609 --> 00:00:41.850
But in February 2012, county officials claimed
they discovered some safety violations and

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:42.899
shut it all down.

00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:47.359
"The county government has issued Eustace
a cease and desist order, telling him to shut

00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:52.379
down his nature school, saying his buildings
don't meet code."

00:00:52.379 --> 00:00:57.530
Conway and his staff were shocked at the county's
sudden crackdown, since he said that the county's

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:00.920
previous inspections hadn't ever found any
problems:

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:06.530
"We've never had anybody hurt by one of the
buildings, we've never had any health issue

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:12.119
here, and so like after 26 years that's a
pretty strong statement."

00:01:12.119 --> 00:01:15.880
He and his staff didn't see how they could
comply with the new demands:

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:22.920
"If we complied to everything that the county
is requesting, we would cease to exist as

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:23.920
we are.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.579
It's just not an option."

00:01:25.579 --> 00:01:29.460
Conway thought he'd been wronged, and took
his fight to the courts.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:35.829
Fortunately, the state stepped in and passed
a law providing an exemption for his school

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:36.829
in 2013.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.380
Not Very Neighborly

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:43.439
About ten months into Conway's dispute with
the county, he got into a fight with his neighbor,

00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:44.909
Margaret A. Palms.

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:49.909
She told The High Country Press that they
were once good friends, until Conway disputed

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:52.869
the property line they'd shared for years.

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:56.170
The argument reached a head in December 2012.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.429
Palms told the Press:

00:01:57.429 --> 00:02:04.039
"He went and tied our gate shut, so we couldn’t
get out and he put posters all over our gates,

00:02:04.039 --> 00:02:05.219
mailboxes, fences.

00:02:05.219 --> 00:02:08.710
Then he put big wooden barriers, so we couldn’t
get out.

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:11.170
He just kind of went nuts."

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.129
But Conway got another good break.

00:02:13.129 --> 00:02:19.569
In May of the following year, The High Country
Press reported that the charges had been dismissed.

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:22.390
Tom Oar's One-Day Audition

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:27.459
People who live off the land are unfairly
stereotyped as being a little crazy.

00:02:27.459 --> 00:02:33.020
But, indeed, some folks who decide to go off
the grid are gifted with more of that special

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:36.450
something that makes for great reality TV.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:41.409
Take Tom Oar, for example: on the recommendation
of Oar's neighbor, Mountain Men followed him

00:02:41.409 --> 00:02:47.180
around for a day before they decided he had
to be on television.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.659
Of course, they probably didn't take into
account some of the things that they might

00:02:50.659 --> 00:02:56.450
have to endure, like follow him on a three-day
hunting expedition whilst carrying 25 pounds

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:58.030
of camera equipment.

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:02.400
If anyone was crazy in this situation, it
might have been the crew.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.530
Oar's Business Boom

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:10.799
Unlike some reality-television personalities,
Tom Oar has adjusted pretty well to his newfound

00:03:10.799 --> 00:03:11.799
fame.

00:03:11.799 --> 00:03:17.670
Selling moccasins, custom knives, and other
wilderness goodies, Mountain Men’s Oar cleans

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:21.020
up, as viewers have started clamoring for
his goods.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:26.140
If you're interested in buying some of it,
however, we have bad news: Oar doesn't have

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:31.760
an internet presence, which means you have
to get your butt to Yaak, Montana, if you

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:34.450
want some genuine merchandise.

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.770
If he's not sold out, that is.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:40.030
Charlie Tucker's House Was A Local Attraction

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:45.220
Before Mountain Men started, Charlie Tucker
was already a local celebrity in North Maine

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.220
woods.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:51.000
Not only did everyone in town know about the
guy who built a cabin with his own hands,

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:55.370
his house was also one of two stops on a day-long
tour.

00:03:55.370 --> 00:04:01.129
After taking the tour themselves, producers
saw in Tucker a "willpower and stubbornness"

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:04.670
that told them he had to be on their show.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:07.180
Protector Of The People

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:12.420
Years before he gained fame on Mountain Men,
Rich Lewis was already hailed as a hero in

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:16.910
Montana for his reputation for mountain-lion
fighting.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:22.840
In 2007, a mountain lion ran amok in Twin
Bridges, Montana, killing two dogs.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:27.530
Had it been left alone, there's no telling
what it would have done next; fortunately,

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:32.990
the Department of Fish, Wildlife, and Parks
reached an agreement with Lewis and set him

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:34.860
loose on the cougar.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:41.169
He took it out before it could harm any other
animals—or worse, someone's child.

00:04:41.169 --> 00:04:43.370
Rich Lewis's Dog Delivery

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:48.730
In season four of Mountain Men, Lewis lost
his best friend, his dog Brandy.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:55.060
Bill Lane, Dan Turner, and Lucas Sims, all
fans of the show, knew they needed to do something,

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:58.500
so they brought him a new canine companion.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:07.110
To make this heartfelt gesture, the trio journeyed
1,700 miles to Lewis' off-the-grid homestead.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.720
It's Good For Local Business

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:13.740
When the History Channel decided to send camera
crews to follow Lewis and Oar through remote

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:18.509
areas of Montana, they probably didn't anticipate
the good it would do.

00:05:18.509 --> 00:05:23.710
Rather than send their own crews out into
the wild, producers hired the local Warm Springs

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:26.919
Productions crew to film the wilderness buffs.

00:05:26.919 --> 00:05:33.910
By 2013, the company employed roughly 70 people
and needed to move into a larger facility.

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:39.130
In addition, Mountain Men led to other gigs,
like filming for the Travel Channel's Making

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:40.660
Monsters.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:42.900
Marty Meierotto: Life Saver

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:48.000
Because of the public's fascination with these
rugged outdoorsmen, newspapers and magazines

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:51.870
have taken it upon themselves to find out
more about them.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.840
This isn't always a good idea.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:06:01.020
Field &amp; Stream magazine sent Bill Heavey to
spend some time with Marty Meierotto.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:06.770
As the writer followed Meierotto around during
an Alaskan winter for three days, he quickly

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:08.560
discovered he was out of his element.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:14.330
At one point, Heavey tried to make it back
to Marty's cabin on his own, and got lost.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:19.750
Luckily, Meierotto knew what he was doing,
and was able to save the reporter from becoming

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:20.750
a popsicle.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:21.750
Thanks for watching!

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:25.020
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:28.611
And leave us a comment to let us know which
Mountain Men fact surprised you the most...

